      "excerpt": "Maristania urban uprisings, no-fly enforcement, and the truces that didn't hold.",
      "body": "March 2012: uprisings ripple through Qiyang cities during the Qiyah Spring. Air patrols enforce brittle no-fly zones while ground factions test how far they can push before someone launches a Koridor CAP.\n\nHistorians argue whether Spring was prelude to Chihebere's 2019 gamble or a separate fault line. Pilots argue about which city had the worst SAM belt. Both are correct.",
